{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1366972-how-would-you-rp-represent-ascended-masters","id":1366972,"title":"How would you RP/represent Ascended Masters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-11T07:34:12-08:00","id":1366972,"title":"How would you RP/represent Ascended Masters?","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> The Ascended Masters are spiritual guides in New Age spirituality that assist others in their journey to spiritual ascension. They are former humans who became spirits, who are called &quot;personages&quot; in M20. However, I don't know if all Ascended Masters could/should fit into the box of personages, and if it's possible for them to be a general spirit. There's also a question: where do they rank? Incarnae? Gaffling? Etc?<br /> <br /> If you had a dreamspeaker trying to covet their favor in your game, how would you represent them?<br /> <br /> A link for reference:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.ascendedmasterindex.com/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.ascendedmasterindex.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> ascendedmasterindex.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.ascendedmasterindex.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.ascendedmasterindex.com/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Find information, resources and relevant links for ascendedmasterindex.com. This domain may be for sale. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.ascendedmasterindex.com/christed.htm\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.ascendedmasterindex.com/christed.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> ascendedmasterindex.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.ascendedmasterindex.com/christed.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.ascendedmasterindex.com/christed.htm </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Find information, resources and relevant links for ascendedmasterindex.com. This domain may be for sale. </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12664,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","user":"KingJohn","date":". 02-11-2020, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T09:22:41-08:00","id":1367002,"title":"","content":"It greatly depends on the role they're supposed to represent.<br /> <br /> For instance, I've toyed with the idea that the fabled Ascended Masters of the new-age migth be...<b>mages </b>- that the whole thing it's a way for the Traditions to interact with humans that believe in magic in a &quot;magical&quot; way w/o revealing all their cards. Cementing ideas of Ascension and that there may be a grain of truth behind all mystical practices to point towards the general &quot;place&quot; Traditions want the Concensus to be<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you had a dreamspeaker trying to covet their favor in your game, how would you represent them? </div> </div> </div>General Spirits seem to suit this role well. They don't need to belong all to one rank, but probably the one's you communicate with aren't of higher rank than Lord. They give me an Astral Umbra vive.<br /> <br /> <b>Lord </b>it's a good rank for a spirit that's powerful and knowledgeable enough that you may want to covet their favor. They're often fully sapient &quot;individuals&quot; with an agendal. Also, Lords often deal with mages to pursue their own interests.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't make them actual &quot;former humans&quot; because in Mage these come either from disembodied mages, or those rare mages that achieved Godhood. And these don't tend to form a <i>hierarchy</i>...except for Treath Null (not the best precedent)...but, in principle, they *could* be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-11-2020, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T05:57:59-08:00","id":1368900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1366972-how-would-you-rp-represent-ascended-masters?p=1367002#post1367002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It greatly depends on the role they're supposed to represent.<br /> <br /> For instance, I've toyed with the idea that the fabled Ascended Masters of the new-age migth be...<b>mages </b>- that the whole thing it's a way for the Traditions to interact with humans that believe in magic in a &quot;magical&quot; way w/o revealing all their cards. Cementing ideas of Ascension and that there may be a grain of truth behind all mystical practices to point towards the general &quot;place&quot; Traditions want the Concensus to be<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> General Spirits seem to suit this role well. They don't need to belong all to one rank, but probably the one's you communicate with aren't of higher rank than Lord. They give me an Astral Umbra vive.<br /> <br /> <b>Lord </b>it's a good rank for a spirit that's powerful and knowledgeable enough that you may want to covet their favor. They're often fully sapient &quot;individuals&quot; with an agendal. Also, Lords often deal with mages to pursue their own interests.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't make them actual &quot;former humans&quot; because in Mage these come either from disembodied mages, or those rare mages that achieved Godhood. And these don't tend to form a <i>hierarchy</i>...except for Treath Null (not the best precedent)...but, in principle, they *could* be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting.<br /> <br /> What kind of powers/abilities would you give certain ones?<br /> <br /> For example, the Goddess of Liberty can supposedly project the powers of the Elohim vis-a-vi her spiritual authority. She also has a &quot;freedom flame,&quot; which is quite nebulous if you ask me.<br /> <br /> Could charms be used to encapsulate the scope of their abilities?<br /> <br /> Goddess of liberty, for reference:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://sirius-eng.net/news/2018/2018-11-30.htm\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://sirius-eng.net/img/logosirius.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://sirius-eng.net/news/2018/2018-11-30.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> THE GODDESS OF LIBERTY </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://sirius-eng.net/news/2018/2018-11-30.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> https://sirius-eng.net/news/2018/2018-11-30.htm </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T06:30:11-07:00","id":1376397,"title":"","content":"Any thoughts? <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T11:19:30-07:00","id":1376417,"title":"","content":"I would need to break out my Mage books to actually look up spirit Charms - and I've got my own project to work on today - but off the top of my head, here are some ideas for powers the Goddess of Liberty could employ.<ul><li>The ability to open any lock and undo every binding. As an embodiment of freedom, she has the power to free the trapped from prison and the enslaved from bondage. With the Goddess of Liberty's blessing, the Mage cannot be tied or cuffed, nor do locked doors provide impediment to her movement.</li> <li>Embolden the spirits of those enslaved. To truly shrug off the yoke of slavery, the bound must have the courage and the might to best their captors, and the cowed must exercise a valor and strength to match their oppressors/tormentors. The Goddess of Liberty can bless a Mage so that, when faced when a physically superior opponent, their Strength based dice pools will grow to match them. Similarly, their Willpower dice pool can increase when dealing with oppressors, or those attempting to compel the Mage to obedience (whether through Intimidation, Coercion, or Mental Control effects).</li> <li>Allow humans the clarity to recognize their sins. Committed to helping mankind ascend by overcoming the weight of their karmic debt, the Goddess of Liberty should have the power to inspire self-awareness on mortals. She might have a Charm that stuns a person for a few rounds, as they are overwhelmed by revelations about themselves, and made to confront long-buried aspects of their thoughts and deeds. Long-term, it might alter the person's behavior, although this is solely up to the character in question. In a more positive light, communing with the Goddess of Liberty may give clues to the Mage in her next Seeking.</li> <li>Illuminate the darkness and banish falsehood. The Goddess of Liberty wields the fire of truth. While this has a more straightforward application (use the &quot;Blast&quot; Charm to do fire damage), it has a more benign application in creating light and destroying illusions.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}